From c528ee2c5423711bfed86ddd2e405d740846ef61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iitimii <timiiowolabi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 17:46:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 18/24] S1a: stream_weights load-path opt-out + common flags

Add llama_model_params::stream_weights, off by default: when set, the
loader suppresses load-time prefetch (posix_madvise WILLNEED) and
populate (Linux MAP_POPULATE), and instead advises the mapping
POSIX_MADV_RANDOM plus MADV_NOHUGEPAGE where available. Weights then
become resident purely on demand-fault, so a later residency manager
can control what stays in RAM.

llama_mmap gains a stream ctor arg with these semantics. It also
gains discard_range(), a pure madvise(DONTNEED) with no munmap and no
fragment bookkeeping, mirroring the align/page-boundary idiom already
used by unmap_fragment.

Any bundle-member load (bundle_prefix set), not only genuinely
streamed ones, suppresses populate too: a non-streamed tier
MAP_POPULATE-ing the whole multi-GB bundle would charge the cgroup
for every other tier's bytes and install PTEs over their regions that
block their own fadvise-based eviction. llama_model_loader grows a
stream_no_populate() helper (stream_weights || bundle_prefix set) and
threads it into init_mappings(). After load_all_data finishes a
bundle-member load, it now sweeps discard_range() over the mapping
outside that model's own [mmap_used.first, mmap_used.second) interval
before the existing unmap_fragment() trims it, so no foreign
page-cache charge survives the load.

llama_model_load gates stream_weights on LLAMA_LOAD_MODE_MMAP and a
single-file model, failing the load with a clear error otherwise.
no_alloc probes (used by -fit's device memory breakdown) are exempt:
they never touch the populate/prefetch path regardless of load_mode,
so gating them produced a spurious error on every default
--stream-weights invocation without changing the outcome.

common_params gains the Phase 5 streaming flags (stream_weights,
max_ram_mib, prefetch_layers, pin_budget, stream_reserve_mib,
stream_disk_gbps, residency_selftest) and matching arg.cpp options
next to --bundle-prefix. common_init_from_params disables warmup when
streaming (weights aren't resident yet by design) with a log line.
residency_selftest is parsed but inert here; a later task wires it up.

Assisted-by: Claude Fable 5
